But observe my laws, abstaining from the things Which thy soul must fear, distinguishing them well; Letting intelligence o'er thy body reign (36);
— *The Golden Verses of Pythagoras*, Perfection, trans. Nayan Louise Redfield (1917), p. 121. **Surface Gloss:** Keep yourself free from the forbidden foods and pollutions prescribed in the rites of purification and soul-liberation, exercising sharp discernment and setting best intelligence above as your charioteer.

**The Input-Charioteer Protocol:** Freedom of mind (*lysis psychēs*) requires two simultaneous controls: (1) **Strict Input Filtering** (ruthlessly abstaining from physical and informational "foods" that muddy your nervous system), and (2) **Executive Steering** (installing cold, high-altitude judgment—*Gnōmē*—in the driver's seat over bodily impulses). Diet without discernment is superstition; discernment with toxic inputs is crippled.
